    "q-221730": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221730",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$ then $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ for any $a,b\\in Z.$ \n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be a pair of integers $a$ and $b$ such that \n\n$$\n{{field-1}}(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-2}}(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "By denoting $P(a)$ and $Q(a)$ as\n\n- $P(a,b):\\,6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\n\n- $Q(a,b):\\,3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀a,b\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q.\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true.\n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true.\n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a,b\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q) & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(P⇒Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(¬P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,P∧¬Q \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,(6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8))\\,∧\\,(3a≢3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be a pair of integers $a$ and $b$ such that \n\n$$\n6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\,\\text{and}\\,3a≢3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
